  '<p class="gd-p">Your booking is confirmed. A few things are left: your licence photos, a selfie and proof of coverage, a signature from each additional driver, and the deposit.</p><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-what-we-still-need-from-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What we still need from you</h2><p class="gd-p">While a request or booking is not complete, everything it still needs is in one list, <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, under the steps on <b class="gd-ui">Trips</b> and on the booking: one line for each thing, with its state and a small button. The red button of <b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b> is always the first thing to do.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Needed</td><td>Send it: press the button on the line</td></tr><tr><td>Not accepted</td><td>We could not accept what you sent: the reason is on the line, send it again</td></tr><tr><td>Under review</td><td>We have it and a person on our team is checking it</td></tr><tr><td>Done</td><td>Nothing more to do</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="gd-p">The lines are what this booking needs: your licence (front and back) and a selfie for each driver, proof of coverage (not with the Protection Plan), signing and paying, the deposit, each additional driver accepting the terms, your date of birth and your home address. On the booking, the details the agreement needs are filled in right there, under <b class="gd-ui">Your details for the agreement</b>. Our reminders name the same things.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-booking-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your booking page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every booking opens with a large photo of your car, its name, the status and a clock: &quot;Pickup in 2 days 4 h&quot;, or &quot;Return by Sun 7 PM&quot; while you have the car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Trips</b>, then your booking. The status is on the photo, for example Confirmed, with your booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under the photo: when and where you pick up and return the car (tap a place to open it in Maps), the kilometres included, the fuel rule and the deposit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b>, at the top, tells you the one thing still needed, with its red button, for example <b class="gd-ui">Upload documents</b>, and the time left before pickup. Under it, your steps: done, now (<b class="gd-ui">Your turn</b>) and later. When nothing is needed it says when and where to pick up the car, with <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Manage your trip holds <b class="gd-ui">Licence and coverage</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Ask to change dates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Message us</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call us</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add a driver</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Cancel booking</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/972"><img src="/guides/img/renter-08-booking-confirmed-desktop-b5603da5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="972"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.4%;top:54.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.4%;top:78.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.4%;top:76.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Money, on the right (below on a phone), shows what you paid and what is owing, part by part, with a <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> button when something is open and your receipts. <b class="gd-ui">Price details</b> opens every line of the price. The steps under <b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b> show how far along you are: approve the offer, sign and pay, licence and insurance, pick up, return, final statement. A step finished since your last visit ticks over as the bar moves.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-rental-step-by-step" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your rental, step by step</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Your rental, step by step</b> on your booking opens the walkthrough: the whole rental in four stages, Before pickup, At pickup, On the road and The return.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start the walkthrough</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Continue</b> once you have begun). The top shows how many steps are done and which stage you are at.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The step to do now is in black at the top. A task opens its page, for example <b class="gd-ui">Add your licence</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Sign the agreement</b>, and is ticked once it is done. A step to read (what to bring, where we meet, your own photos, the road rules, what to do if something goes wrong, how to bring the car back) has <b class="gd-ui">Got it</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">At pickup, the walk-around: we photograph the car with you and you sign the condition report on your phone. Once done, <b class="gd-ui">See the photo report</b> opens every photo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every stage is listed below with its steps, so you can read ahead.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-upload-your-licence-selfie-and-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Upload your licence, selfie and coverage</h2><p class="gd-p">Do this at least 24 hours before pickup. It takes a few minutes with your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Upload documents</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Licence and coverage</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Licence, front: lay the licence on a dark surface with all four corners visible. Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Choose from my photos</b> for a photo already on your phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Licence, back: do the same for the back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Selfie with your licence: hold the licence beside your face, then press <b class="gd-ui">Take selfie</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Coverage for damage to the car: add what your option asks for, then press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Choose from my photos</b> (a PDF works too). Not sure your credit card covers rentals? Use the card coverage checker first.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">While your booking still needs them, <b class="gd-ui">Your trips</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Upload your licence</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Upload proof of insurance</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Check if your credit card covers rentals</b>, and our request and offer emails link straight to the licence upload.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/verify</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1232"><img src="/guides/img/renter-09-verify-desktop-d20f668d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1232"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.5%;top:65.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:63.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:81.2%;top:63.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:95.3%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Your option</th><th scope="col">What we need</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Option 1, OPCF 27 on your own policy</td><td>Your insurer, the policy number and its expiry (after your return date), then two pages: your <b class="gd-ui">pink slip</b> (the liability insurance card) and the <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 endorsement page</b>, each a PDF or a photo. Send both before you pay: the payment opens once they are in.</td></tr><tr><td>Option 2, your credit card&#39;s rental coverage</td><td>Pay with that card: it must be a credit card (debit and prepaid cards are refused) in your name. Search for your card (the bank and the card&#39;s name) and pick it: the page tells you at once whether it covers this car (the card&#39;s value limit, the kinds of car it leaves out, the most days). Then tick and confirm. Not on the list? Tick <b class="gd-ui">My card is not on the list</b> and type its name: our team checks it. The card&#39;s benefits document is optional.</td></tr><tr><td>Option 3, the CarmaCars Protection Plan</td><td>Ask for it on your booking; we confirm it once it is active.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Which cards include rental car coverage? <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span> lists them, with each card&#39;s car value limit (MSRP), its longest rental and a link to its guide. Most cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and some of our cars are priced higher. Only your card&#39;s issuer decides a claim: call the number on the back of your card before you rent.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A person checks your proof and approves it, or tells you what to fix. The car is handed over only once it is approved. Changing your option replaces the earlier proof. We remind you 48 and 24 hours before pickup while it is missing. We delete licence and face photos 90 days after your rental ends.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-additional-drivers" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Additional drivers</h2><p class="gd-p">Each additional driver signs the agreement with their own link.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When the agreement is ready, each driver with an email gets their own signing link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Copy their signing link</b> to send it yourself, or <b class="gd-ui">Send a new link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each driver adds their own licence photos and selfie, like you did.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Signing links expire after 72 hours. A new link ends the older one, so always send the newest.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-add-something-to-your-trip" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add something to your trip</h2><p class="gd-p">Until 24 hours before pickup (or the notice an add-on needs), add add-ons from your booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, under Add-ons, press <b class="gd-ui">Add something to your trip</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tick the add-on you want. Its price shows below.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add and pay</b>. It is charged at once on the card you paid with, and shows on your booking and receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A chauffeur needs our confirmation: press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for it</b>. We confirm it and charge your card then.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">No card on file for this booking? The add-on is added and waits for payment: press <b class="gd-ui">Pay for your add-ons</b> under Add-ons, enter a card and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>. It is charged at once; that card is not kept.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>If you cancel, add-ons are refunded like the rest of your booking. Flowers and a chauffeur are not refunded once their notice before pickup has started.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-what-to-bring-to-pickup" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What to bring to pickup</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Your original licence. A photo is not enough.</li><li>The card you paid with. The deposit is taken on it about an hour before pickup.</li><li>A few minutes to walk around the car with us. We photograph it together.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-check-in-yourself-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check in yourself (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">From 24 hours before pickup, <b class="gd-ui">Check in yourself</b> on your booking: take the photos of the car as you get it (pick them all at once from your camera roll: all sides, odometer, fuel gauge, inside, any damage), the odometer and the fuel. If your booking is ready, you are checked in at once; otherwise a team member confirms it. If you do not take the photos, we take them.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-if-we-change-your-coverage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If we change your coverage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">If your card does not cover the car, or you ask for the CarmaCars Protection Plan, our team can switch your booking for you. You get an email with what changed and the new total. On an offer you approve the new price. On a booking you have paid, any extra is sent to you as a secure payment link, or you pay it from your booking page. You then do not need to send a card coverage document. If you go back to your card, the booking page asks you to confirm it again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-accident-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your accident card</h2><p class="gd-p">Your booking shows your <b class="gd-ui">Accident card</b>: what to do after an accident, and the coverage of this booking.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>With your own auto policy (OPCF 27): your insurer and policy number, as on the proof you uploaded.</li><li>With your credit card coverage: the card and its coverage provider.</li><li>With the Protection Plan: the provider, the policy number, the claims phone and your plan reference.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Print it</b> to print the card at its size for the glovebox, or keep the page on your phone.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Your name and date of birth</h3><p class="gd-p">Set them in your profile. Once your licence is verified they must match it: a change is sent as a correction request, shown as waiting until our team checks it against your licence.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-if-your-card-does-not-cover-the-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If your card does not cover the car</h2><p class="gd-p">The page says why: the card has no rental car damage coverage, the car is worth more than the card&#39;s limit, the card leaves out this kind of car, or the rental is longer than the card allows. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Use OPCF 27 on my policy instead</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Ask for the Protection Plan</b> just below.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('renter', 'after-your-trip', 'chapter', 'during-your-trip', 'We check the car with you at the return. Your deposit balance comes back, and your receipts and agreement stay in your portal.

## The return and your deposit

- At the return we check the odometer, fuel or charge, keys and cleanliness, take photos and compare with pickup. You sign on our screen.
- The photo report of the pickup and the return is in your email, in Documents and on your booking (**Photo report**): the times, the kilometres, the fuel, every photo and any damage. A late return, kilometres over the allowance or less fuel than at pickup are charged from these readings.
- We release the deposit balance after you return the car. If a toll, ticket or claim is still open, we may hold back what we expect it to cost for a while.
- Your statement appears under Documents.

## Review your trip

After the return we send you a link by email or text. It takes about a minute, and we help you write it.

1. Open the link. Tap what you liked: the car, the pickup or delivery, communication, the price, cleanliness, how easy booking was, or the name of the person who helped you.
2. If you like, tap the stars for how it felt, and write one sentence in your own words.
3. Your review appears, made only from what you picked and wrote and the facts of your booking. Change anything you like.
4. Press **Post on Google**: it copies your review and opens Google. Choose your stars and paste it. **Copy** only copies it.

Already left a review? Press "I already left a review" and we stop asking. Something wasn''t right? The page offers to tell us directly. We never offer anything for a review, and every renter gets the same link.

## Review your rental on our site

1. Open the trip under Past trips, then press **Review your rental**. Liked the car? **Book again** opens it for new dates.
2. Tap the stars. Add a title and a few words if you like. Both are optional.
3. Tick **Show my review on the site with my first name** only if you agree to it being shown.
4. Press **Send my review**.

![](/guides/img/renter-14-review-desktop-c6c61830.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 672; address: carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10004/review; pins: 2 25.0 33.6, 3 3.5 84.5, 4 18.1 92.4")

## Documents and your account

The menu has four links: **Trips**, **Documents**, **Rewards** and **Account**.

1. **Documents**: your agreements, receipts, statements and uploads. Press **View** or **Download**.
2. **Account** > **Profile**: your contact details (**Save**), sign-in, drivers and your Card on File.
3. **Account** > **Notifications**: notices from us. Use **Mark as read** or **Mark all as read**, and choose which optional emails you get. A number on **Account** in the menu is how many notices you have not read.

![](/guides/img/renter-15-documents-desktop-fd428a63.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/account/documents; pins: 1 91.8 35.7")

> Tip: Your legal name is locked once you are verified. To change it, call or message us. To change your email, open Profile, Sign-in and press **Change my email**: we send a link to the new address and tell the old one, and the email changes when the link is opened.

## Sign in with your phone number

No password needed: we text you a 6-digit code from the CarmaCars number.

1. On `carmacars.ca/sign-in`, press **Use my phone number instead**.
2. Enter your mobile number and press **Text me a code**. Codes go to Canadian mobile numbers.
3. Type the 6-digit code from the text (on most phones it fills itself in), or press **Sign in**. The code works for 5 minutes; **Send a new code** after a minute if it did not arrive.
4. To sign in by phone every time, open **Account** > **Profile**, press **Add and verify my phone number**, enter the code we text you, then choose **My phone number (a code by text)** under Sign in with. The sign-in page then opens on your phone number.

> Tip: New here? On Create account, press Sign up with my phone number instead: your name, your mobile number and the code. An account made by phone has no email yet: you can send requests, accept offers and sign, and the pay page asks for your email before your first payment, for the receipts. A booking request you sent earlier with the same mobile number is added to your account once the code is checked.

## Texts or email: how we reach you

Choose Email, Text or Both. Texts are short, come from the CarmaCars number and link to the page.

1. Open **Account** > **Profile**. Under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both**. It is saved at once.
2. Texts go to the phone you verified with a code (Sign-in, above). Until you verify one, we email you.
3. Signed agreements, statements and receipts are always emailed when we have your email. On Text you also get a text with a link to view or download them.
4. No texts from 9 pm to 8 am, except urgent ones such as a late return. Reply STOP to any text to stop texts (we confirm with one text); text START to turn them back on.

> Tip: You can also choose in the booking request (How should we reach you?) and when you sign up with your phone number, where Text is chosen for you.


## Rewards

Open **Rewards** in your account.

1. Every rental earns 1 point per dollar of the rental charge when it closes. 100 points are worth $1 off the rental charge of a later booking.
2. More ways to earn are listed on the page: refer a friend with your link (you both get points at their first rental), follow us, review your rental on carmacars.ca, review us on Google (press **I posted my review** and give the name on it), a damage-free rental, your birthday and your first rental.
3. **Get my code** turns points into a code of your own, from 500 points. Type it in the promo code box of your request. An unused code can be given back for the points.
4. Rent 10 days in 12 months for Silver (5% off) and 30 for Gold (10% off): your tier code is on the page.
5. Points end 12 months after your last rental or redemption. We email you a month before.

## Your trip in your calendar or wallet

On a confirmed booking, **Add to calendar** adds the pickup and the return. The confirmation email has the same link. **Add to Apple Wallet** shows when it is available.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert on your phone or computer when your offer is ready, before pickup and return, for payments and when we message you, even with CarmaCars closed.

1. Open **Account** > **Profile**. Under **Phone alerts**, press **Turn on alerts** and allow notifications when your browser asks.
2. Under **What to alert me about**, untick anything you do not want. Your choice applies to all your devices.
3. Press **Send a test alert** to see one. **Turn off on this device** stops them there; **Remove** takes another device off.

On iPhone and iPad, add CarmaCars to your Home Screen first: in Safari tap **Share**, then **Add to Home Screen**. Open CarmaCars from your Home Screen, sign in and turn alerts on in Profile (iOS 16.4 or later).

> Good to know: Alerts come as well as your emails and texts, never instead of them. Alerts that are not urgent wait until 8 am. Sign-in links and codes never come as alerts.

## Delete my account

1. Open **Profile** and scroll to **Delete my account**.
2. Press **Delete my account**, add a reason if you like, then **Yes, delete my account**.
3. We settle anything still open (a rental, a deposit), delete your account and email you within 30 days. Changed your mind before then? Press **Keep my account**.

> Good to know: We keep rental agreements, receipts and tax records as the law requires. Everything else, including your licence and selfie photos, is deleted.

## Odometer and fuel at pickup and return

When you check the car in or out yourself:

1. Add a photo of the dashboard (the odometer and the fuel gauge). It can come from your camera roll. We read it and ask, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel level.
2. Take a selfie in front of the car with your camera.

After the return, **Your return: km and fuel** on your booking shows the km driven, the km included and any km over, the fuel compared with pickup, and the charge for each. The photo report shows both dashboard photos.

## Earn reward points

Review your rental (add a photo for extra points), review us on Google, follow us from your Rewards page, refer a friend, and every rental after your first earns points too. See them all on **Rewards**.

## Rewards and fuel (release 35)

- Earn points for a photo with your review and for every rental after your first; every way to earn is on your Rewards page.
- A fuel shortfall at the return is priced from the car''s tank and the local pump price, plus a refuelling fee, and checked by our team before any charge.', 'After your trip', 'The return, your deposit, reviews, documents and your profile.',
